# Charts, Pusher & API Server

## Charts (`modules/charts/`)

- Entry: `modules/charts/index_new.js` → `htbCharts` in bot.js
- Uses patched Highcharts renderer + Puppeteer/Chromium (Docker: `PUPPETEER_EXECUTABLE_PATH`)
- Member charts triggered by `getMemberChart` intent in bot.js
- License: `ACCEPT_HIGHCHARTS_LICENSE=YES` in Dockerfile

## Pusher notifications

Flow: `helpers/pusher-htb.js` (parse HTML) → `helpers/notification-router.js` (route/filter/queue) → `DISCORD_ANNOUNCE_CHAN_ID`

| Module | Role |
|--------|------|
| `helpers/pusher-htb.js` | Pusher client, `parsePusherEvent()`, logs via `createLogger("pusher-htb")` |
| `helpers/notification-router.js` | Announce queue, `@mentions`, cache debounce, fallback poll, captain history/repost |
| `helpers/notification-store.js` | Postgres `seven_notification_events` — append/list/repost source rows |
| `helpers/pusher-config.js` | `PUSHER_*` env toggles |

- Pusher subscribes at startup (before Discord `ready`); pending announces queue until channel is fetched
- Own filter: team member **or** first blood **or** linked Discord account
- Fallback: `getRecentMemberActivities()` when Pusher unhealthy (`PUSHER_FALLBACK_POLL_MS`); poll also runs while healthy
- Persist: `NotificationRouter.recordEvent()` → `NotificationStore.append()` (all paths incl. skipped)
- Boot: `importDbBackup()` → `NOTIFICATION_STORE.ensureSchema()` → `NOTIFICATION_ROUTER.initFromStore()`
- Admin: `admin.pusherStatus` / `seven pusher status` (connection + 25-item memory buffer)
- Captain: `captain.pusherHistory` / `captain.pusherRepost` — DB history + `handleOwnEvent({ forceRepost: true })` (no stat re-integration)
- Local NLP: patterns in `helpers/nlp.js` (`pusher history`, `pusher repost last|<id>`)
- Dev: `IS_DEV_INSTANCE=true` appends to `LOG_DIR/PUSHER_MSG_LOG.json` (Docker) or `cache/PUSHER_MSG_LOG.json` (local); replay via `npm run test:pusher`
- Event formats: `docs/developer/pusher-events.md`

## Optional API server

Only active when `API_SERVER_ENABLED=true`:
- `modules/seven-api-server.js` — Express + passport-discord
- Requires `API_SERVER_PORT`, `API_SERVER_URL`, Discord OAuth credentials
- Do not document these vars as required in env templates
